class.description:
A child of a [CharacterBody3D] (or of any [CollisionObject3D], see [member body_path]). Every physics frame, while the body moves at [member auto_min_speed] or more (or the controller gives [method set_intent]), it looks for a ledge in the way: a wall within [member reach_distance] of the body's capsule (read from its first [CollisionShape3D]; a capsule, cylinder, box or sphere), facing the way the body goes within [member max_wall_angle]; a top no steeper than [member max_ledge_slope] between [member min_height] and [member max_height] over the body's feet; room for the capsule on the top, straight up in front of the wall and over the edge. A thin obstacle (its far side within [member vault_max_depth], a landing beyond it) is vaulted when there is no room on it, or when the body runs at [member vault_min_speed] or more. A ceiling over the body lowers the heights searched; a ledge the body could walk under (a beam over head height) is left to [method try_mantle].
The mantle moves the body itself, each physics frame, along a path from the ledge's geometry: up in front of the wall until the capsule is over the top, then onto it (a vault goes over and down beyond it), turned to face the wall when [member align_to_wall] is on; a [CharacterBody3D]'s velocity follows the motion, and is [member exit_speed] into the ledge at the end. A collider that moves (an [AnimatableBody3D] platform) carries the ledge with it. The body's own controller should not move it while [method is_active] is [code]true[/code] (the traversal sets the body's transform after the body's own physics processing, as its child).
The pose: a [FellowTraversalPose3D] on the character's [Skeleton3D] reaches the hands for the edge, puts the feet on the wall's face and onto the top and tips the torso towards the wall over whatever animation plays; or plays the clip set for the kind ([member low_clip], [member high_clip], [member vault_clip]) across the mantle, its root's motion ([member clip_root_bone]) warped onto the ledge as the body's path. The signals tell an [AnimationTree] when to switch. See [code]docs/decisions/0180-traversal-mantling.md[/code].
Hanging (milestone 75): in the air, a ledge the body cannot climb (no room on its top: a wall rising behind it, an overhang) whose edge is about [member hang_reach] over its feet is caught and hung from ([member hang]; with [member hang_first], every ledge it could climb too, or [method try_hang]): the body hangs below the edge facing the wall, moves along it as the intent goes left or right ([member shimmy_speed]), following it as it turns and steps and stopping where it ends, at a gap or at something in the way; it climbs when pushed at the wall again, up, or [method climb_up] (a mantle from the hang), and lets go when pulled away, down, or [method release]. Ladders: a [FellowLadder3D] the body goes towards ([member ladders]) is climbed at [member ladder_speed] (the intent up or towards it: up; [method set_climb_input]), stepped off at its foot, and at its top mantled off onto what is there. The pose puts the hands on the edge or the rungs and the feet on the wall or the rungs.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# A controller: the input as the intent, nothing while the traversal moves the body.
func _physics_process(delta):
    if $FellowTraversal3D.is_active():
        return
    var wish = Vector3(input.x, 0, input.y) * speed
    $FellowTraversal3D.set_intent(wish)
    velocity.x = wish.x
    velocity.z = wish.z
    move_and_slide()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// A controller: the input as the intent, nothing while the traversal moves the body.
public override void _PhysicsProcess(double delta)
{
    var traversal = GetNode<FellowTraversal3D>("FellowTraversal3D");
    if (traversal.IsActive())
    {
        return;
    }
    var wish = new Vector3(input.X, 0, input.Y) * Speed;
    traversal.SetIntent(wish);
    Velocity = new Vector3(wish.X, Velocity.Y, wish.Z);
    MoveAndSlide();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
